l": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Ichiko+Aoba+Sayonara+Penguin", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/6781124419", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Ichiko+Aoba+Sayonara+Penguin", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Ichiko+Aoba+Sayonara+Penguin&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2026 hermine"]}, {"t": 6317, "time": "01:45:17", "artist": "Prymek & Sage", "title": "Hill Blocks View", "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://prymekandsage.bandcamp.com/track/hill-blocks-view", "search": false}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Prymek+%26+Sage+Hill+Blocks+View", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Prymek+%26+Sage+Hill+Blocks+View", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Prymek+%26+Sage+Hill+Blocks+View", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Prymek+%26+Sage+Hill+Blocks+View", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Prymek+%26+Sage+Hill+Blocks+View", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Prymek+%26+Sage+Hill+Blocks+View&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["“this one here is from an album called Shelter by Primack and Sage and this one here is called Hill Blocks View”", "Lead single from Chaz Prymek & Matthew Sage's duo album 'Shelter' (AKP Recordings, 2026); 'Primack and Sage' is an ASR mishearing of Prymek & Sage."]}, {"t": 6840, "time": "01:54:00", "artist": "Lukas Bueno Jr", "title": "Move Your Heart", "conf": "low", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Lukas+Bueno+Jr+Move+Your+Heart", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Lukas+Bueno+Jr+Move+Your+Heart", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Lukas+Bueno+Jr+Move+Your+Heart", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Lukas+Bueno+Jr+Move+Your+Heart", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/1604425559", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Lukas+Bueno+Jr+Move+Your+Heart", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Lukas+Bueno+Jr+Move+Your+Heart&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2022 Lukas Bueno Jr"]}, {"t": 6962, "time": "01:56:02", "artist": "Mark Wayne", "title": "Children at the Playground, Pt. 10", "conf": "low", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Mark+Wayne+Children+at+the+Playground%2C+Pt.+10", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Mark+Wayne+Children+at+the+Playground%2C+Pt.+10", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Mark+Wayne+Children+at+the+Playground%2C+Pt.+10", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Mark+Wayne+Children+at+the+Playground%2C+Pt.+10", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/1586815339", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Mark+Wayne+Children+at+the+Playground%2C+Pt.+10", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Mark+Wayne+Children+at+the+Playground%2C+Pt.+10&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2022 Good Karma Sounds"]}, {"t": 7027, "time": "01:57:07", "artist": "Hannah Frances & Mary Lattimore", "title": "Beholden to the Birds Murmuring Above", "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Hannah+Frances+%26+Mary+Lattimore+Beholden+to+the+Birds+Murmuring+Above", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Hannah+Frances+%26+Mary+Lattimore+Beholden+to+the+Birds+Murmuring+Above", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Hannah+Frances+%26+Mary+Lattimore+Beholden+to+the+Birds+Murmuring+Above", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/track/4rJDJnOFLms2b4oFquIBFg", "search": false}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Hannah+Frances+%26+Mary+Lattimore+Beholden+to+the+Birds+Murmuring+Above", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Hannah+Frances+%26+Mary+Lattimore+Beholden+to+the+Birds+Murmuring+Above", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Hannah+Frances+%26+Mary+Lattimore+Beholden+to+the+Birds+Murmuring+Above&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["“Hannah Francis is the artist... it's called Beholden to the Birds Murmuring Above”", "Instrumental collaboration with harpist Mary Lattimore, on the deluxe edition of Hannah Frances' 'Nested in Tangles' (Fire Talk, 2026)."]}, {"t": null, "time": "--:--:--", "artist": "Andrew Tuttle & Darren Cross", "title": null, "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://andrewtuttle.bandcamp.com/album/at-dc", "search": false}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Andrew+Tuttle+%26+Darren+Cross", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Andrew+Tuttle+%26+Darren+Cross", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Andrew+Tuttle+%26+Darren+Cross", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Andrew+Tuttle+%26+Darren+Cross", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Andrew+Tuttle+%26+Darren+Cross", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Andrew+Tuttle+%26+Darren+Cross&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["“that really beautiful, peaceful song from Andrew Tuttle and Darren Cross that Mara left us with from the bridge”", "mentioned by the presenter but we couldn't work out when it played", "Real Brisbane/Sydney duo collaboration album 'AT/DC' (Room40/Someone Good, 2026); presenter didn't name the specific track played, so title is left unknown."]}], "counts": {"high": 16, "mid": 11, "low": 3}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:00:35", "end": "00:01:12", "text": "You're listening to In The Pines on FBi Radio. For some reason the intro is not playing for you but that's fine, I'm going to talk it for you. My name's Johanna Roberts, this is the show that is all things country and folk, leaning on the cosmic side of things and to start us off, a bit of a bump after that really beautiful, peaceful song from Andrew Tuttle and Darren Cross that Mara left us with from the bridge. This is Brennan Weddle with Let's Be Models."}, {"start": "00:09:37", "end": "00:11:12", "text": "Brand new music there from Babe Hoven. That's their latest. It's called Lasagna. Before that, we had Orville Peck with Too Little Too Late and that is taken from his forthcoming album. It is called Mule and the record, I'm very excited about this record, partly because of the guests that are being featured on it. So it's obviously Orwell Peck and his last couple of releases, he had a lot of, you know, duets and features and that kind of thing. But on this new record, we're going to have accompaniment from Alison Russell, Noah Cyrus and Emmylou Harris as well, which is very exciting. And at the top of all of those songs to start us out on the show, we had the excellent Brennan Weddle with her latest Let's Be Models. and she has an album coming out soon as well, which I think is going to be a real stunner. My name's Johanna Roberts. This is In the Pines on FBI Radio, 94.5 FM. And I'm playing you all kinds of cosmic country and folk to see you through your Tuesday night, so do stick around. It's going to be a good time. This one here is a new one. Look, you might see a trend here. Lots of new music for you tonight. pretty much everything is a very recent release with one or two exceptions and this one here is from Anna Graves it's called Goldmine"}, {"start": "00:18:10", "end": "00:18:44", "text": "And Harry was a butcher, Loretta did the books, and Conrad was their only son, and I was born to be a clerk. I trained to be a teacher, but I couldn't find the work, and I just wasn't cut out."}, {"start": "00:22:53", "end": "00:23:18", "text": "Hit Club 77 with a new generation of talent, our FBi Radio dance class of 2026. For eight weeks, our dance class graduates have been busy learning DJ skills, radio presenting and readying themselves for a club night. You're invited to Club 77, Friday, July 31, from 10pm till late, to witness the launch of the next generation of DJs. Catch Asira."}, {"start": "00:27:08", "end": "00:29:20", "text": "You're listening to In The Pines with Johanna Roberts here on FBi Radio 94.5 FM. Of course, you might be listening to us on digital or streaming us via our website. There are so many ways that you can get hold of FBi these days. Of course, our website, I keep thinking of it as our new website, but it's been like this for a little while now. You can find us online at fbi.radio. and there's all sorts of things on that website you can apart from just streaming us live which is a great thing to be able to do you can also listen back to shows they're all archived there in the schedule you can check out playlists you can find out all sorts of things happening in the community and most importantly as always you can sign up to become a supporter of the station we are a community station we do rely on supporters and donations to literally keep us up and running make sure that we have microphones that work the electricity bill gets paid all of those sorts of things so if you have been thinking about signing up as a supporter or making a donation anything over two dollars is tax deductible and that includes those monthly supporter payments so if that's something that pushes you over the line I think that's not a bad thing to consider so fbi.radio is where you can go for all of those things in that set of songs i should tell you what we were just listening to um we started out with anna graves and her latest gold goldmine followed it up with houndmouth from their new album lordy and rodeo was the song that we heard a taste of the new lamb chop album as well the two songs so far have been really beautiful and that one there was called The New World Wave and just at the end there, Joanna Samuels featuring Jordan Lenning with Full Story. This is In the Pines and this is a good country song for you. It's from John R. Miller from his new record, The Great Unknowing. This one's called Day Drinking."}, {"start": "00:46:09", "end": "00:47:34", "text": "Maddy Diaz there, featuring alongside Lucy Dacus with an un-unplugged version of her song Heavy Metal. Before that, we had Ken Pomeroy with Deportee, which is a protest song originally by Woody Guthrie that I have heard, I think, about three covers of lately. and unsurprisingly it is unfortunately continues to be a really timely song you know the words of Woody Guthrie are still resonating through to today which is on the one hand you know it's wonderful that music continues to be listened to many many years after the fact however it's also a bit disheartening when certain sentiments are just as applicable today as they were you know 50 or 60 years ago and we also had Lily Mayola with I Want To from her album Lucky To Be and John R. Miller at the top with Day Drinking. You're listening to In The Pines with Johanna Roberts here on FBI Radio and this one here is a new one from local artist Jordan Wilson featuring Maya Yelovic and it's called When We Meet. You're with Johanna Roberts on In the Pines."}, {"start": "01:01:05", "end": "01:02:07", "text": "You're listening to In The Pines on FBi Radio just there. The great new one from Lottie McLeod. It's called Wednesdays at the Waterloo. Before that we had Squirrel Flower with Not Me, Rayland Baxter with The Fool. I feel like it's been a while since we've had music from him. I feel like I also say that a lot about artists with only really the reference that to me I haven't been across new music lately. so he might have been putting out music that I just haven't been aware of but it is really nice to have something from Rayland Baxter. That one was called The Fool and we started out with Jordan Wilson and Maya Yelovic with When We Meet. My name's Johanna Roberts. As I mentioned, this is In the Pines, the Cosmic Country and Folk Show here on FBI Radio and this one here from their beautiful new album Sweet Thief. for this is Le Look with the closing track, Homesick in LA."}, {"start": "01:15:43", "end": "01:19:26", "text": "Gwenifer Raymond there from her album Last Night I Heard the Dog Star Bark, a record that came out last year and I somehow was completely oblivious to it despite the fact that I've really enjoyed earlier records of hers. But, yeah, it's a really extraordinary record, this one, and that is a track from it called Jack Parsons Blues, and that is in reference to the, I want to say infamous, Jack Parsons, who was a rocket scientist and also a devotee of the occult, which I think is an interesting combination. and he basically, yeah, he worked for early stages of NASA when it was like the jet propulsion laboratory and he also ran the California arm of Alistair Crowley's sex magic cult and his life also intersected with L. Ron Hubbard before he started Scientology. So that is all to say that that really beautiful witchy song also is in reference to a really interesting witchy guy, I guess, as well. So if you're interested in that, look, you could do worse than to look into Jack Parsons' life. And Gwennifer Raymond, she is playing a show that I also only just heard about, and it is sold out because it's in a relatively small venue here in Sydney. But yeah, look, it's sold out, but there might be, I guess, maybe keep an eye on it in case tickets become available. She is playing on Wednesday, the 26th of August at Lazy Thinking. And I think there might actually have been a second show that was just added. I'm literally finding this information as I talk to you. But yeah, I believe a second Sydney show because of how quickly the Lazy Thinking show Sold Out is happening at the Vanguard on the 25th of August and I think that'll be a really extraordinary show. Before Gwenefa Raymond we had Field Commander Ali with She Was Picking Flowers and we started out with Lelook and Homesick in LA. My name's Johanna Roberts. This is In the Pines on FBI Radio and while I have just been talking a lot at you I do have one more thing that I want to tell you about and that is a bit of a departure from what you're hearing on in the pines tonight but i did want to let you know that it is dance class finale club night coming up pretty soon very very soon actually because it's happening this friday july 31st i am alarmed that it's the end of july already but this is a very nice way to ring out the month so basically um come to club 77 and witness the new generation of talent our fbi radio dance class of 2026. For eight weeks our graduates have been busy learning DJ skills, radio presenting and getting themselves ready for a club night. So you're invited to Club 77 Friday the 31st of July from 10pm till late to witness the launch of the next generation of DJs. So you'll be able to catch Saira, Westrider, Snowpig, Harsa, Calyx and Sorbonne at this Club 77 launch night and you can get your tickets now through Resident Advisor and it is all proudly sponsored by Absolute Vodka and Create New South Wales. I'm going to play you something now that is decidedly not for the club but a good time nonetheless this one here is from tasha it's called lucky"}, {"start": "01:29:59", "end": "01:30:34", "text": "You're listening to In The Pines with Johanna Roberts and just there we had Chateau with Man of the Country, followed on from Lorraine and Every Age and at the top we had Tasha with Lucky which is from her new album You Are Spring. it is oh half past 10 we're really getting on tonight i've got a few more songs to play for you including this one here uh which is it's called auto smile the artist is called at and if you're looking them up it's literally just the at symbol"}, {"start": "01:44:27", "end": "01:45:17", "text": "A thoroughly charming new song there from Ichiko Aoba. It is called Sayonara Penguin and the little penguin squeaks in the background of the song are also vocalised by her and yeah, it's very, very sweet. Before that, we had Jude Brothers with Desire and Devotion and we started out with Auto Smile from At. You're listening to In The Pines with Johanna Roberts here on FBi Radio. I'm going to play you something now from we're going to get into a little bit of an instrumental mode as we get towards the end of the show this one here is from an album called Shelter by Primack and Sage and this one here is called Hill Blocks View"}, {"start": "01:55:18", "end": "01:56:06", "text": "This is Primack and Sage and Hill Blocks View, bringing us up to the end of another night's In The Pines. My name's Johanna Roberts. It has been a great pleasure, as always, having your company on a Tuesday night between 9 and 11pm. It is, however, getting on up for 11, which means it is time for me to vacate the studio. But I've got one last track to take us through. This one is from the deluxe version of her album, Nested in Tangles. Hannah Francis is the artist. This particular track features the wonderful Mary Lattimore and it's called Beholden to the Birds Murmuring Above. Do stay tuned. Surfacing is up next."}], "fbi_json": [{"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:01:08"}, "track": {"title": "Let's Be Models", "artists": [{"name": "Brennan Wedl"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_